<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yuwen Jue</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">542–557</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Emperor Xiaomin of Northern Zhou</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yuwen Jue was the first ruler of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/northern-zhou">Northern Zhou</a>, son of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-wei">Western Wei</a> regent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuwen-tai">Yuwen Tai</a>. In 557 his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yuwen-hu">Yuwen Hu</a> forced the last Western Wei emperor to abdicate in his favour, and he took the archaic title Heavenly King of Zhou. When he tried to remove Yuwen Hu later that year, he was deposed and killed.</p></div>
